/* pj_vtap: the "voltage tap" of the pcbjam live engine (design: docs/features/simulation/).

   A code part (a chip whose behaviour is a program, run through d_cosim) cannot see a
   voltage: d_cosim has digital ports only. This model is the part's eyes. It has analog
   inputs and no outputs; after every time step ngspice has accepted it hands the voltages
   on its inputs to the engine (ngspice_live.cpp), which keeps the last two steps and
   answers the part's question "what was the voltage on my input k at time t" by drawing a
   straight line between them.

   id      the number of the code part these voltages belong to (the part's own call-order
           number, the same one its d_cosim model gets as "irreversible")
*/

NAME_TABLE:

C_Function_Name:       cm_pj_vtap
Spice_Model_Name:      pj_vtap
Description:           "hands voltages to the pcbjam live engine after each accepted step"

PORT_TABLE:

Port_Name:             in
Description:           "the voltages to hand over"
Direction:             in
Default_Type:          v
Allowed_Types:         [v,vd,i,id,vnam]
Vector:                yes
Vector_Bounds:         [1 -]
Null_Allowed:          no

PARAMETER_TABLE:

Parameter_Name:     id
Description:        "number of the code part these voltages belong to"
Data_Type:          int
Default_Value:      0
Limits:             [0 -]
Vector:             no
Vector_Bounds:      -
Null_Allowed:       yes
